5: //! references and selected members along one path. The classifier follows that
6: //! path in the raw type graph instead of inferring sibling object members and
7: //! function parameters.
8: //!
9: //! A classification state identifies the module that owns a raw reference, the
10: //! value or instance side used for member lookup, and the unconsumed member
11: //! path. Named-member traversal examines only members declared directly on the
12: //! current type. A member available only from a base type is therefore
13: //! indeterminate. A pending member path may cross a non-generic concrete class
14: //! created by `new` without inspecting its constructor arguments.
15: //! Function-return classification has one narrower inheritance case: an
16: //! interface with no call signature may follow its single base interface.
17: //! Traversal visits at most 1024 distinct classification states. Unsupported
